close_reason: Aligned public bulk rollback types and runtime admission with checkpoint identities
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_strengthened
  gate_id: packed-bulk-rollback-option-contract
  negative_control: "The original published SDK rejects rollback checkpoint strings and accepts useless booleans; pnpm smoke:npx now compiles positive checkpoint-ID and negative boolean assignments through the installed package."
  local_checks[3]: pnpm typecheck,"pnpm smoke:npx",node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/runtime/runtime-input-bulk.spec.ts
  hosted_checks[2]: Gates (coverage),Release readiness
  owner: pm-gh1564
body: "**Version:** 2026.10.23. **Scope:** core exported `PmBulkMutationControlOptions`, `PmUpdateManyActionOptions` and `PmCloseManyActionOptions`. **Severity:** low SDK correctness / recovery authoring friction.\n\nIn the scratch package, compile this file:\n\n```ts\nimport type { PmUpdateManyActionOptions,\n  PmCloseManyActionOptions } from '@unbrained/pm-cli';\nconst update: PmUpdateManyActionOptions = { rollback: 'update-many-checkpoint' };\nconst close: PmCloseManyActionOptions = { rollback: 'close-many-checkpoint' };\nconsole.log(update, close);\n```\n\nCommand: `npx tsc --noEmit --strict --skipLibCheck --module nodenext --target es2023 --types node bulk-types.ts`.\n\n**Observed:** two TS2322 errors: string is not assignable to boolean or undefined. Replacing strings with true compiles, but passing those option bags to `PmClient.run('update-many', { options })` / `run('close-many', { options })` does not request rollback. The former reports no mutation flags; the latter reports missing close filters. The boolean does not name a checkpoint and is dropped from rollback dispatch.\n\nCLI help correctly declares `--rollback <value>`, and the lower-level `runUpdateMany`/`runCloseMany` structured option declarations correctly use string. Those working APIs provide a workaround; the defect is the exported flat bulk action types, not absence of SDK recovery.\n\n**Expected:** type rollback as a checkpoint ID string, sharing the runtime contract. Reject boolean inputs with a rollback-specific diagnostic instead of dispatching as an ordinary forward bulk operation. Add a packed-consumer type check accepting actual checkpoint IDs for both action types.\n\n**Measured cost:** the two compiler diagnostics occupy **196 bytes / 49 estimated tokens**. The accepted-boolean runtime control required two dispatcher calls and returned refusal strings rather than performing recovery: its compact serialized error objects total **737 bytes / 184.25 estimated tokens**. Compilation failure is not a successful restore. No state loss occurred in this control.\n\n**Duplicate searches**, same all-state limit-20 command:\n\n- `\"rollback\" \"boolean\"`\n- `\"PmBulkMutationControlOptions\"`\n- `\"PmUpdateManyActionOptions\"`\n- `\"PmCloseManyActionOptions\"`\n- `\"rollback\" \"SDK\"`\n- `\"rollback\" \"type\"`\n- `\"rollback\" \"checkpoint\" \"typing\"`\n\nNo matching exported-rollback-type report found. Results include broad SDK/preview and workspace restore reports, not this boolean/string declaration mismatch. This draft is distinct from Draft 1's actual rollback state semantics."
